==Battleground==
*Infinite [[UltraBaaBaa]]s spawn after 0.07 seconds<sup>2f</sup>, delay 23.33~30 seconds<sup>700f~900f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Gabriel]]s spawn after 10 seconds<sup>300f</sup>, delay 23.33~30 seconds<sup>700f~900f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Helmut Krabbe]]s spawn after 10 seconds<sup>300f</sup>, delay 40~46.67 seconds<sup>1,200f~1,400f</sup>.
*1 [[Sunfish Jones]] spawns as the boss after 33.33 seconds<sup>1,000f</sup>.
*5 [[Angelic Gory|Angelic Gories]] spawn after 50 seconds<sup>1,500f</sup>, delay 26.67~33.33 seconds<sup>800f~1,000f</sup>.
*3 [[UltraBaaBaa]]s spawn after 50 seconds<sup>1,500f</sup>, delay 6.67~8 seconds<sup>200f~240f</sup>.
*1 [[Winged Pigge]] spawns after 86.67 seconds<sup>2,600f</sup>.
*3 [[UltraBaaBaa]]s spawn after 100 seconds<sup>3,000f</sup>, delay 6.67~8 seconds<sup>200f~240f</sup>.
*1 [[Mini Angel Cyclone]] spawns after 120 seconds<sup>3,600f</sup>.

==Strategy==
This stage focuses more on [[:Category:Angel Enemies|Angel Enemies]] than [[:Category:Alien Enemies|Alien Enemies]], so you should focus mainly on [[:Category:Anti-Angel Cats|anti-Angel units]], though [[Fencer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|The Kitty of Liberty]] is still worth bringing. Using "[[Resistant]]" Effect UP [[Cat Combo]]s and [[Rocker Cat (Rare Cat)|Ramen Cat]] are a good combination for stalling Winged Pigge and the other Angels. Using [[Horror Movies (Combo)|Horror Movies]], [[Biohazard (Combo)|Biohazard]] and [[Bony Bone (Combo)|Bony Bone]] is the best option if you're having trouble with stalling. As for attackers, [[Phantom Cat (Rare Cat)|Bubble Cat]], has [[Immune to Weaken]] and [[Massive Damage]] against Angels, making him an amazing option. Additionally, because Winged Pigge spawns on a timer and Sunfish Jones has a low magnification, it's possible to rush the base before Winged Pigge spawns using anti-angel [[Massive Damage]] units like [[Food Stall Cat (Rare Cat)|Cafeteria Cat]], or heavy-hitting cats like [[Talents|Talented]] [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]].

==='''Recommended Ubers'''===
*[[Dioramos (Uber Rare Cat)|Ascendant Dioramos]]: He destroys this stage as it was more than likely built as a testing ground for him. He has Knockback + Slow against both the Angel and Alien enemies on this stage, combined with Barrier Breaker, he hard counters every enemy except for Winged Pigge. To deal with her, be sure to bring Ramen Cat, as a steady stream of them can permastall her.
*[[Mizli (Uber Rare Cat)|Mizunade]]: On this stage, she's essentially Dioramos if he traded Angel targeting for spammability and lower cost. A great choice, but like him, protect her well from Winged Pigge's Weaken.
*[[Kalisa (Uber Rare Cat)|Divine Kalisa χ]]: A great Anti-Angel rusher whose base damage is solid as well. She also only barely outranges Winged Pigge's Omni Strike, so try to use the Thunderbolt Cannon so she lands at least one good hit.

==Trivia==
*Like [[Pursuit of Understanding]] and [[1 + 2 = Tor]], Isosceles Valley appears to have been designed specifically for one of the [[Ultra Form]]s added in [[Version 13.0 Update|Version 13.0]] alongside [[Demon of Deciliter Bay]]. In this case, Isosceles Valley is ideal for [[Dioramos (Uber Rare Cat)|Ascendant Dioramos]], who can knockback and slow all enemies in the stage with his added [[:Category:Alien Enemies|Alien]] target and pre-existing [[:Category:Angel Enemies|Angel]] target, is guaranteed to break [[UltraBaaBaa]]'s [[Barrier]], is immune to [[Sunfish Jones]]'s Slow ability, and has a Resist Weaken [[Talents|Talent]] for [[Winged Pigge]].
*Prior to [[Version 13.2 Update|Version 13.2]], [[Winged Pigge]] was buffed to 250% instead of 150%.
*On the map, this stage, combined with the previous four, outlines an isosceles triangle.

